course: dictionary
lesson: 4081
title: Many meanings of get
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Get» is a small word with lots of jobs. It can mean receive, become, arrive or understand. The words around it tell you which job it is doing. «You can't get burnt when it's cloudy,» says your big sister. Burnt comes after get, and the clue is that you become burnt, so get means become here.
explain: Try swapping in another word and see if the sentence still makes sense. «Animals can get trapped in plastic rings.» If you swap in become, it reads «Animals can become trapped», which still makes sense, so you have found the meaning.
explain: Some uses of get are casual, like talking with friends. «I've got three» means «I have three». The formal voice of writing uses other words instead, such as «obtain» or «receive». «Scary predictions online are usually nonsense meant to get attention» means they are meant to obtain attention.
fact: Get is a verb, and its forms are get, gets, got, getting and gotten or got.
fact: «Get» can mean receive, become, arrive or understand, depending on the words around it.
fact: «Get» can mean become, as in «get wet», «get better», or «get tangled».
fact: «Get» can mean catch, as in «get a cold» or «get the bus».
fact: In casual talk, «got» often means «have», so «I've got three» means «I have three».
exercise: «Animals can get trapped in plastic rings.» In this sentence, get means | sleep | sing loudly | throw away | *become
exercise: Dad says, «Hurry, we need to get the bus.» Here, get means | bury | hide | *catch | throw
exercise: Nadia says, «I get it!» What does she mean? | She has caught a cold | *She understands | She is getting a present | She is arriving home
test: «Older children often help a lot, but if it gets too much, tell a parent.» What does gets mean here? | understands | arrives | receives a gift | *becomes
test: In «Scary predictions online are usually nonsense meant to get attention», which formal word could replace get? | sleep | dance | forget | *obtain
exam: Which sentence uses get to mean receive? | *Mia will get a birthday present from her gran. | Mia will get lost in the park. | Mia will get wet in the rain. | Mia will get up early.
